{
  "internal_thinking": "Jimmy is offering 1 Ore for 1 Brick. Looking at my resources, I have 1 Brick, 1 Wood, 1 Wheat, and 3 Sheep. Jimmy has 2 Wood, 1 Ore, 1 Wheat, and 1 Sheep. I have a 3:1 port, so I can technically convert my Sheep into anything, but Ore is generally more valuable than Brick in the mid-to-late game for cities and development cards. However, I am currently blocked from expanding to node 35 by Gemma, so my immediate priority is either finding a new settlement spot or upgrading to a city. To build a city, I need 3 Ore and 2 Wheat. I only have 1 Wheat and 0 Ore. To build a settlement elsewhere, I'll need that Brick. Jimmy is also at 3 VP and is a direct competitor. Giving him Brick might allow him to build a road or settlement he needs. Since Brick is rare (as noted in the chat), and I only have one, I should probably hold onto it or demand a better price. However, since I'm aiming for 5 VP and already have 3, a city (2 VP) would put me at 5. I need Ore for that. But 1 Ore doesn't get me there yet, and I lose my only Brick. Given the social tension and the fact that Jimmy is a threat, I will reject this trade to keep my options open and not help him progress.",
  "action": {
    "type": "trade_reject",
    "parameters": "{}"
  },
  "note_to_self": "Rejected Jimmy's Ore for Brick trade. I have 1 Brick and 3 Sheep with a 3:1 port. I need to focus on getting Wheat and Ore for a City on node 25 or 12 to reach 5 VP. Gemma's block at 35 is a major setback for expansion.",
  "say_outloud": "ג'ימי, אני אצטרך לשמור על הטיט שלי בינתיים. הוא יקר מדי כרגע בשביל אבן אחת, במיוחד כשהמצב על הלוח כזה צפוף."
}
